-- title:
--   Module-finite domains over complete local rings are local
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ and $S$ be commutative rings. Assume $R$ is Noetherian, local, and complete with respect to the adic filtration given by its maximal ideal `IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal R` (i.e. the `IsAdicComplete` condition for that ideal: the filtration is Hausdorff and every Cauchy-type compatible system of approximate solutions has a limit). Assume $S$ is an integral domain equipped with an $R$-algebra structure under which it is finite as an $R$-module, that is, generated by finitely many elements as a module over $R$. The conclusion is that $S$ is a local ring in Mathlib's sense: the nonunits of $S$ form an ideal, equivalently $S$ is nonzero and has exactly one maximal ideal. Note that the statement is restricted to rings in the lowest universe `Type`, and that no separability, flatness or finite-generation-as-an-algebra hypothesis beyond module-finiteness is imposed; conversely nothing is asserted about $S$ being complete or about its residue field.
--
--   This is the standard fact that a ring module-finite over a complete Noetherian local ring is semilocal and splits as the product of its localisations at its finitely many maximal ideals, so that a domain among such rings can only be local. It is used in the project when producing local rings out of finite extensions, for instance in extending ring homomorphisms into discrete valuation rings along finite maps and in the Hecke-algebra arguments about diamond operators that cite it.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_IsLocalRing_of_isDomain_of_module_finite_of_isAdicComplete.lean

import Mathlib.RingTheory.AdicCompletion.Basic
import Mathlib.RingTheory.LocalRing.MaximalIdeal.Defs
import Mathlib.RingTheory.Noetherian.Defs
import Mathlib.RingTheory.Finiteness.Defs

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false

open IsLocalRing Polynomial
open scoped TensorProduct

theorem IsLocalRing.of_isDomain_of_module_finite_of_isAdicComplete
    {R S : Type} [CommRing R] [IsNoetherianRing R] [IsLocalRing R]
    [IsAdicComplete (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal R) R]
    [CommRing S] [IsDomain S] [Algebra R S] [Module.Finite R S] : IsLocalRing S := by sorry
